<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">United States of Indonesia</h1><p class="st-meta">1949 CE – 1950 CE · capital Jakarta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Federal state to which the Netherlands transferred sovereignty in 1949, dissolved within months into the unitary Republic of Indonesia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-indonesian-round-table-conference">Round Table Conference</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> in 1949 ended the Indonesian revolution with a compromise. On 27 December 1949 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> to the Republic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, a federation of sixteen states that joined the revolutionary Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> with states set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-east-indonesia">East Indonesia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-pasundan">Pasundan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> became president and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-hatta">Mohammad Hatta</a> prime minister under a federal constitution, linked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> in a loose union. Many Indonesians saw the Dutch-created states as colonial puppets, and the attempted coup by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-westerling">Raymond Westerling's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a> forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandung">Bandung</a> in January 1950 discredited federalism further.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>One by one the member states voted to merge into the Republic, and on 17 August 1950 the federation was replaced by the unitary <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Resistance in the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a>, which proclaimed a separate republic, was suppressed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-states-of-indonesia.jpg" alt="United States of Indonesia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Jayakatwang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1949 CE – 1950 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jakarta</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sukarno, Mohammad Hatta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Indonesian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of the United States of Indonesia, RIS</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=united-states-of-indonesia" aria-label="United States of Indonesia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7639 2408 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United States of Indonesia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7959 2664L7959 2664M7959 2664L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7959 2664h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7959 2664h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7959 2664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Jakarta. <a href="/atlas?year=1950&amp;focus=united-states-of-indonesia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
